    "body": "@yuri1969 \r\n\r\nThanks for your answer. I'm trying to figure out a way to make Starship work on all my hosts with the same configuration (so I can keep them all in sync automatically).\r\n\r\nIn other words I want to remove this snippet of config:\r\n\r\n```ini\r\n[username]\r\nshow_always = true\r\n\r\n[hostname]\r\nssh_only = false\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe issue is that `su -` clears my environment variables, including `SSH_CONNECTION`, so Starship no longer realizes I'm connected remotely and stops displaying the hostname:\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/597206/70391560-ccecfb00-19d6-11ea-8f17-8c15a3d3707a.png)\r\n\r\nAny thoughts?\r\n\r\nA potential fix would be to check if the current terminal session is a child of a `sshd` process, rather than relying on `SSH_CONNECTION`.\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/597206/70392093-5b17b000-19dc-11ea-8ead-2a04bcdafb16.png)\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/597206/70392095-5eab3700-19dc-11ea-9c71-5a0957083db1.png)\r\n",
